# Location, Maps, and Tracking

- Use provider abstractions for geocoding, routing, mapping, and tracking-related external services.
- Latitude/longitude are first-class delivery location data and must be validated for valid ranges.
- Driver tracking is operationally scoped to active delivery context according to product rules.
- Never expose unnecessary historical driver-location data.
- Store timestamps with every authoritative location event.
- Treat GPS as an input with uncertainty; do not assume every coordinate is exact.
- Provider API keys MUST remain server-side when the architecture requires it; mobile-public keys must use provider restrictions and documented configuration.
- Route calculations should not be embedded in unrelated domain classes.
